      "worked_solution": "Let us call $x$ the exterior angle of $\\angle F.$ Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is $360^{\\circ}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{100}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{78}^{∘}+{62}^{∘}+x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {300}^{∘}+x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={360}^{∘}-{300}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
